# ── Deployed environments ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are two Netlify sites, each with its OWN environment variables and its
# OWN database. Nothing is shared between them.
#
#   PROD  https://starlit-biscuit-dbe6ae.netlify.app   -> production database
#   DEV   https://beautiful-sprite-a18e5b.netlify.app  -> development database
#
# They deliberately do not share AUTH_SECRET, so a session or mobile token
# issued by one is rejected by the other. That is the reliable way to tell which
# environment you are actually talking to.
#
# Keep this local file pointed at the DEVELOPMENT database. Pointing it at
# production makes localhost — and the Android debug APK, which targets your
# machine — write to the client's real books.

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neon / Supabase / any PostgreSQL connection string.
# sslmode=verify-full keeps full TLS verification and silences the pg
# deprecation warning about what "require" will mean in pg v9.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dairy_billing?sslmode=verify-full"

# ── Auth (NextAuth v5) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Each environment gets its OWN secret. This also signs the Android app's bearer
# tokens (src/lib/mobile/token.ts), so changing it signs out every phone too.
AUTH_SECRET="your-secret-here"

# The URL this instance is served from — localhost for local work, and the
# matching Netlify site URL above in each deployed environment.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Admin seed credentials (used only for prisma/seed.ts) ───────────────────
ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@dairy.local"
ADMIN_PASSWORD="change-me-on-first-login"

# ── Encryption key for sensitive DB fields (WhatsApp API token) ──────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# IMPORTANT: Set once in production (e.g. Netlify env vars) and never change it.
# Changing it invalidates all encrypted tokens stored in the database.
ENCRYPTION_KEY="your-32-byte-hex-key-here"

# ── WhatsApp webhook verify token (for /api/webhooks/whatsapp) ───────────────
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN="your-webhook-verify-token"

# ── Green API credentials are stored in the DB via Settings page ─────────────
# No environment variables needed for Green API.
